# The Belligerent (5/5 Vehicle, Crew 3; "whenever it attacks, create a Treasure token. Until end of turn, you may look at the top card of your
# library any time, and you may play lands and cast spells from the top of your library"). Turn 1: four Moxen pay {2}{U}{R}; the three Memnites
# are cast for free. Turn 3: the Memnites crew it (total power 3) and it attacks. With the trigger on the stack Bot1 may neither look at the top
# card nor cast the Lightning Bolt on it. Once it resolves Bot1 has a Treasure, may look (CR 401.2), and casts the Bolt off the top for its
# mana cost - Mox Ruby's {R} - but not the Shock on top of Bot2's library ("your library"). In the second main phase it plays the
# Forest that is now on top as its land for the turn, casts the Ornithopter under it, and may not play the Island beneath as a second land
# (CR 305.2). On turn 5 the effect has ended ("until end of turn"), covered by the next scenario.
# CR 111.10a, 611.2a, 305.1, 601.3.

